# Windows batch files must keep CRLF endings and are read by cmd in the OEM
# codepage, so they must also stay plain ASCII. `scripts/electron.cmd` broke
# on both counts once already: LF endings plus a UTF-8 dash in a REM comment
# made cmd try to run part of the comment as a command.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
